<title>LITHUANIA: COMMERCIAL BANK POSTS 7.7 MLN LITAS NET PROFIT.</title>
<headline>COMMERCIAL BANK POSTS 7.7 MLN LITAS NET PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first seven months of 1997</p>
<p>(all amounts in million litas unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  7.7	 vs losses 103.5</p>
<p>    Assets		893	 vs	  730</p>
<p>    Total deposits	705.2     vs	  544.8</p>
<p>    Individual deposits 84.2	vs	   80.9</p>
<p>    Loan portfolio	574.7     vs	  607.3</p>
<p>    Special provisions  258.4     vs	  267</p>
<p>NOTES - The comparison figures for assets, total deposits,</p>
<p>individual deposits, loan portfolio and special provisions are</p>
<p>compared to the beginning of 1997.</p>
<p>Lithuania's State Commercial Bank is one hundred percent</p>
<p>state owned and has been slated for privatisation.</p>
<p>The bank reported earlier that its net profit for the first</p>
<p>half of 1997 was 6.1 million litas.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
